.TH EESSI-ARCH-GUARD 1 "" "eessi-arch-guard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eessi-arch-guard \- reload an EESSI module stack that was loaded for another CPU or GPU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eessi-arch-guard
[\fB\-\-shell\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-chain\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-\-syslog\fR \fITARGET\fR]
[\fB\-\-restore\fR]
.br
.B eessi-arch-guard \-\-check\-submit
(\fB\-\-partition\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-constraint\fR \fINAME\fR] | \fB\-\-target\fR \fITARGET\fR)
[\fB\-\-eb\-stack\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B eessi-arch-guard \-\-check\-mount
[\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-site\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-eessi\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-modulepath\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-mountinfo\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-input\fR]
.br
.B eessi-arch-guard \-\-check\-revision \-\-stat
\fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-min\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slurm TaskProlog. When the loaded EESSI CPU or accelerator target is not the
target of the node, it prints export and unset lines for the reloaded module
environment, which slurmstepd applies before it runs the task.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR
Print bash assignments for eval, not prolog lines.
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Exit 78 on a failed decision or an unexpected exception.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Evaluate the configuration, chain, probes and decision without writing state.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one line of JSON with schema_version 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-chain\fR \fIPATH\fR
Run an existing task prolog first.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR
Bound the decision. The default is 60 seconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-syslog\fR \fITARGET\fR
Send structured RFC 5424 or journald decision events.
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR
Read a JSON restore request on standard input and write the JSON result.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-submit\fR
Check LOADEDMODULES against a mapped target without changing it, with
\fB\-\-partition\fR, \fB\-\-constraint\fR, \fB\-\-target\fR and \fB\-\-eb\-stack\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-mount\fR
Say whether the EESSI repository is on a cvmfs mount and the site module
directory precedes the EESSI one on MODULEPATH. Exit 0 when both hold, 1 when
one fails, 2 on a usage or read error. Options: \fB\-\-repo\fR, \fB\-\-site\fR,
\fB\-\-eessi\fR, \fB\-\-modulepath\fR, \fB\-\-mountinfo\fR, \fB\-\-require\-input\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-revision\fR
Read the output of cvmfs_config stat from \fB\-\-stat\fR \fIFILE\fR, print the
client revision, and exit 1 when it is older than \fB\-\-min\fR \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the usage text.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
eessi-arch-guard.conf
Site configuration beside the binary.
